; The tag-set idiom as CDDL generics — the Cardano ledger's `set<T>` / `nonempty_set<T>` /
; `nonempty_oset<T>` bases, which move from hand-written externs to generated types once the idiom is
; recognized — pinned here on the EXPLICIT `@duplicates preserve` opt-out.
;
; The collapse happens at parse time, BEFORE the generic machinery, so a
; `set<a0> = #6.258([* a0]) / [* a0]` choice-bodied generic def stores the already-collapsed Array
; body (a non-collapsed choice-bodied generic def would otherwise hit the finalize-time is_enum
; panic). Each instance resolves to a transparent alias (`pub type SetU64 = Vec<u64>;`), and a field
; typed as an instance serializes through that alias identically to the non-generic equivalent — the
; generic and non-generic paths converge on one resolution.
;
; These generic defs carry `; @duplicates preserve` DELIBERATELY: tag 258 is the IANA set tag, so a
; no-directive 258 idiom now DEFAULTS to `@duplicates reject`. This fixture is the OPT-OUT contract at
; the GENERIC-def level — `preserve` on the def restores the plain `Vec`/`NonEmptyVec` alias and, per
; instance, rides instantiation unchanged (a live corpus pin that the opt-out propagates through every
; instantiation path, complementing the in-process pins in
; `robustness_tests::duplicates_on_generic_def_rides_instantiation`). The reject DEFAULT on generic
; defs is exercised by tag_set_reject.cddl (`oset<a0> … ; @duplicates reject`) and
; tag_set_reject_anon_generic.cddl.
;
; Instances span uint / text / bytes / a struct-typed element so transparent-alias resolution is
; exercised across element kinds; `nonempty_oset` is the third in-the-wild base (conway + dijkstra
; ledger CDDL) proving the mechanism covers N rules, not a hardcoded two. The BYTES element also
; carries this fixture's share of the LIST-DOOR ABI contract: `bytes` is a wasm-bindgen scalar whose
; bare `Vec` is NOT ABI-legal, so its restricted list wrapper must enter through the loose
; `BytesList` class rather than a `Vec<Vec<u8>>` argument — a door spelled the other way generates
; at exit 0 and fails the wasm crate's own compile (E0271), which is what this fixture's wasm-face
; compile cell now catches. The narrow contract is pinned in-process by
; `integration_tests::bytes_and_bool_element_list_doors_compile_and_round_trip`; the rust-side bytes
; collapse (incl. per-element StringEncoding preservation) by
; `optional_tag_set_tests::bytes_element_set_collapses_with_elem_encodings`.
set<a0> = #6.258([* a0]) / [* a0] ; @duplicates preserve
nonempty_set<a0> = #6.258([+ a0]) / [+ a0] ; @duplicates preserve
nonempty_oset<a0> = #6.258([+ a0]) / [+ a0] ; @duplicates preserve
point = [x: uint, y: uint]
holder = [a: set<uint>, b: nonempty_set<text>, c: nonempty_oset<point>, d: nonempty_set<bytes>]
